module gunbc.plans.m5_fixture_store_consolidation

import gunbc.plan { Plan, DissolutionTrigger, HasTrigger }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock, TableBlock, AlignNone }
import gunbc.plans.md_helpers { h2, h3, p, li, li_blocks, ul, ol, cell, row }

fn m5_fixture_store_consolidation_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    p(text: "Node: `node://adhoc-3efc6449-ec5` · MODEL-FIRST SPIKE (escalate before load-bearing). Anchor: DESIGN.md §2 (one concept, every scale — Realization pattern), §3 (single authority, interface↔transport split), §5 (fail-closed). `ROADMAP.md` §2 *Minimal work — caching by realization*."),
    h2(text: "1. The fork"),
    p(text: "Two seeds each hand-roll a fixture store that answers the *same* question — \"given an operation and its inputs, return the recorded response, fail-closed if absent/stale\":"),
    TableBlock {
      header: row(cells: [
        cell(text: "axis"),
        cell(text: "v1 `RecordedFixture` (`src/v1/stage0/src/recorded_fixture.rs`)"),
        cell(text: "v2 `EffectIoFixtureStore` (`src/v2/extdeps/runtimes/v2_effect_io_pure.dag`)"),
      ]),
      alignments: [AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone],
      rows: [
        row(cells: [
          cell(text: "key"),
          cell(text: "`(operation, input_hash = content_hash(inputs))`"),
          cell(text: "`Symbol` locator — degenerate `^effect_io_pure_default_locator` pin (ignores the `RuntimeValue` arg)"),
        ]),
        row(cells: [
          cell(text: "key class"),
          cell(text: "**ContentAddressedByValue**"),
          cell(text: "**HandAuthoredString** (fail-open: distinct args silently alias)"),
        ]),
        row(cells: [
          cell(text: "value"),
          cell(text: "`response: serde_json::Value` (faithful `Value` serialization)"),
          cell(text: "`RuntimeValue`"),
        ]),
        row(cells: [
          cell(text: "placement"),
          cell(text: "on-disk `\{root\}/\{op_slug\}/\{hash\}.json` — **PerHostFilesystem**"),
          cell(text: "in-process `Map<Symbol, RuntimeValue>` — **InProcess**"),
        ]),
        row(cells: [
          cell(text: "read verify"),
          cell(text: "stores `inputs`, verifies on lookup (collision safety) — **content_verified_on_read**"),
          cell(text: "none"),
        ]),
        row(cells: [
          cell(text: "fail-closed"),
          cell(text: "`Missing` / `Stale` / `InputMismatch` / `Expired` / `ResponseDrift` (purity oracle)"),
          cell(text: "miss → rejected; backend mismatch → rejected"),
        ]),
        row(cells: [
          cell(text: "eviction"),
          cell(text: "`Ttl` (FIXTURE_FRESHNESS_SECS = 30d)"),
          cell(text: "`Never` (drops with eval)"),
        ]),
      ],
    },
    p(text: "They are **not two concepts**. They are ONE artifact kind — *a wet-captured effect response, keyed by the content hash of the operation inputs* — realized at two placements. v1 is the mature content-addressed handler; v2 is an immature in-process handler whose key derivation is an explicitly-gated fail-open stub (`effect_io_pure_locator_identity`, dissolve-on: \"derive fixture keys from RuntimeValue→Node reification\")."),
    h2(text: "2. The kernel already exists — `std.cache_interface`"),
    p(text: "This is not a new kernel. DESIGN/ROADMAP already declare the content-addressed cache kernel, and the fixture store maps onto it cleanly:"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "`ArtifactIdentity<T> \{ subject_digest: ContentHash, artifact_kind \}` **is** the `(operation, input_hash)` key — `subject_digest = content_hash(inputs)`, one new `artifact_kind = \"hermetic_fixture\"`."),
      li(text: "`CacheLookupResult<T> = Hit\{receipt\} | Miss | RejectedHit\{reason\}` **is** the lookup outcome."),
      li(text: "`CacheRejectReason` already covers most of v1's fail-closed variants (mapping below)."),
      li(text: "`CacheInterfaceFacts` (locality / key_derivation / lookup·write·miss semantics / eviction / `content_verified_on_read`) **is** the per-handler descriptor — exactly the shape `parse_table_memo.dag` and `resolved_graph.dag` already cite in `extdeps/realization/`."),
    ]),
    p(text: "So the fixture store is a *missing pair of `CacheInterfaceFacts` rows + a shared lookup fold*, not new vocabulary. This spike lands the rows; §5 escalates the fold."),
    h3(text: "Fail-closed reason mapping (the §5 win)"),
    TableBlock {
      header: row(cells: [
        cell(text: "v1 `FixtureError`"),
        cell(text: "kernel surface"),
      ]),
      alignments: [AlignNone, AlignNone],
      rows: [
        row(cells: [
          cell(text: "`Missing`"),
          cell(text: "`Miss`"),
        ]),
        row(cells: [
          cell(text: "`Stale` (operation / input_hash mismatch)"),
          cell(text: "`RejectedHit\{ SubjectDigestMismatch \}`"),
        ]),
        row(cells: [
          cell(text: "`InputMismatch` (stored inputs ≠ current — collision)"),
          cell(text: "`RejectedHit\{ ContentDigestMismatch \}`"),
        ]),
        row(cells: [
          cell(text: "`InvalidDigest`"),
          cell(text: "`RejectedHit\{ BackendKeyMalformed \}`"),
        ]),
        row(cells: [
          cell(text: "`Io` / `Json` / `ClockUnavailable`"),
          cell(text: "`RejectedHit\{ BackendUnavailable \}`"),
        ]),
        row(cells: [
          cell(text: "`Expired` (TTL)"),
          cell(text: "**GAP** — no expiry variant in `CacheRejectReason`; expiry is `eviction: Ttl` but v1 treats it as a *loud refusal*, not a silent evicted-Miss. Needs a `FreshnessExpired` reject reason (or an explicit policy that TTL-expiry is fail-closed)."),
        ]),
        row(cells: [
          cell(text: "`ResponseDrift` (re-record ≠ stored for same key)"),
          cell(text: "**GAP (write path)** — this is the `WriteSemantics = WriteOnce` purity-oracle violation; the kernel has no write-outcome coproduct yet."),
        ]),
        row(cells: [
          cell(text: "`DeserializationMismatch` / `UnknownTag` / `UnreplayableValue`"),
          cell(text: "**GAP (transport faithfulness)** — value (de)serialization faithfulness of the `StructuredArtifact` transport encoding; handler-internal, but worth a typed `transport_encoding`-level reason rather than a stringly reason."),
        ]),
      ],
    },
    p(text: "These three gaps are the model work the load-bearing follow-up adds to `std.cache_interface` **before** the folds are rewired (so the rewire never has to fall back to a stringly error)."),
    h2(text: "3. What this spike lands (NON-load-bearing — additive only)"),
    ol(items: [
      li(text: "`dag/extdeps/realization/hermetic_fixture.dag` — the two cited `CacheInterfaceCatalogFacts` rows (`hermetic_fixture_file_facts`, `hermetic_fixture_in_process_facts`), parallel to `parse_table_memo.dag` / `resolved_graph.dag`. They describe each handler **as it is today** — the fork shows up as a key_derivation divergence (`ContentAddressedByValue` + `content_verified_on_read` vs `HandAuthoredString` + not)."),
      li(text: "`dag/std/cache_identity.dag` — one additive `hermetic_fixture_artifact_kind` data decl (the shared artifact-kind both handlers realize). No fold touched (the only `match` over `CacheInterfaceProduct` is untouched)."),
      li_blocks(blocks: [
        p(text: "`dag/test/claim/hermetic_fixture_realization_test.dag` — executing witness:"),
        ul(items: [
          li(text: "file handler is the content-addressed reference;"),
          li(text: "in-process handler is the fork **today** (RED-on-fabricated-convergence — fails closed if the row is marked converged before the fold lands);"),
          li(text: "both share kernel invariants (same value-shape, `MissIsDiagnostic` fail-closed);"),
          li(text: "one `ArtifactIdentity` routes to **both** backends — §2 \"one spec → N handlers\", executed."),
        ]),
        p(text: "Verified green by execution; perturbing the in-process row to `ContentAddressedByValue` / `content_verified_on_read: true` turns it RED (discriminating)."),
      ]),
    ]),
    p(text: "No existing consumer changes; no Rust touched; no v2 fold touched."),
    h2(text: "4. The convergence target (what closes the fork)"),
    p(text: "The shared key is `subject_digest = content_hash(inputs)`. v1's interim `content_hash_service_inputs` (value_hash limbs) and v2's symbol pin both dissolve onto **`v2.std.node` content_hash over the reified operation-input `Node`** — one digest authority, used by both handlers. When v2's `effect_io_pure_locator_identity` derives the key from `RuntimeValue→Node` content_hash, the in-process row's two divergent fields flip and the fork is gone (the witness then expects the new state — its RED guard converts to the convergence assertion)."),
    h2(text: "5. The load-bearing FOLD that changes — ESCALATE before touching"),
    p(text: "The rewire that makes both stores *dispatch through* the kernel (not just be described by it):"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**v1**: `eval_service_call` in `src/v1/stage0/src/v1_interpreter.rs` (the M4 hermetic-realization fold) calls `RecordedFixtureStore::lookup → Result<RecordedFixture, FixtureError>` and matches the bespoke error enum. Rewire: the v1 handler returns `CacheLookupResult<Value>` and the fold consumes the shared coproduct. `recorded_fixture.rs` `FixtureError` collapses onto `CacheRejectReason` (+ the three new variants from §2)."),
      li(text: "**v2**: the effect dispatch in `src/v2/compiler/05_eval.dag` / `v2_effect_io_pure.dag::effect_io_pure_store_lookup` returns `Outcome<RuntimeValue>`. Rewire: lookup returns `CacheLookupResult<RuntimeValue>`, eval maps it to `Outcome`."),
    ]),
    p(text: "Both are load-bearing seed/substrate folds (`v1_interpreter.rs`, `recorded_fixture.rs`, `05_eval.dag`, `v2_effect_io_*`). Per the project spirit and the M5 brief, the design is escalated to the operator (via parent `calm-wren-408`) **before** any of this is implemented. Sequencing:"),
    ol(items: [
      li(text: "(this PR) cited rows + artifact-kind + witness — non-load-bearing, merges to anchor the model."),
      li(text: "(escalated) add the three `std.cache_interface` gap surfaces (`FreshnessExpired`, write-outcome coproduct, transport-faithfulness reason) — model-first, additive."),
      li(text: "(escalated, signed-off) rewire v1 fold → `CacheLookupResult`; collapse `FixtureError`."),
      li(text: "(escalated, signed-off) v2 value-derived key + rewire v2 fold; in-process row converges; HTTP host door + emitted-host DryRunMode ride this seam (the M5 brief's remaining scope)."),
    ]),
  ]
}

data m5_fixture_store_consolidation_plan: Plan = Plan {
  slug: "m5-fixture-store-consolidation",
  title: "M5 — Fixture-store consolidation onto one Realization kernel",
  body: m5_fixture_store_consolidation_body(),
  dissolution: HasTrigger {
    text: "Delete this doc when the v1 and v2 fixture stores both dispatch through `std.cache_interface` (the §5 fold rewired, `FixtureError` collapsed onto `CacheRejectReason` with the `FreshnessExpired` / write-outcome / transport-faithfulness gaps closed) and the in-process row has converged to `ContentAddressedByValue` + `content_verified_on_read` — at which point \"one fixture concept, two handlers\" is a witnessed property (the convergence assertion green by execution) and this tracker is redundant."
  }
}
